{%- comment -%}
	payment-marks — the accepted payment marks (brief of 22 Oct): Apple Pay,
	Google Pay, Visa, Mastercard and American Express, in that order, each
	shown only while checkout accepts it (shop.enabled_payment_types). Checkout
	also takes Diners Club, Discover and JCB; Tom kept the row to these five
	so it stays one line in the drawer on a 375 px phone. The artwork is
	Shopify's own (payment_type_svg_tag) at its native 38 x 24 and is never
	recoloured, cropped or stretched. Acceptance only: the row is a plain
	list, never a link or a button, with no hover state, and the wallets
	themselves are met at checkout. Each SVG keeps the title Shopify gives it;
	the title's id carries `id_scope`, so the buy box and the drawer can both
	sit on the kit page without repeating an id. Marks only: the line that
	once ran under them went with the spacing brief of 22 Oct.
	Params:
		classes    — wrapper classes (spacing, alignment). Optional.
		id_scope   — word that keeps the SVG title ids unique per placement.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
	assign pm_scope = id_scope | default: 'marks'
	assign pm_id_prefix = '"pi-' | append: pm_scope | append: '-'
	assign pm_types = 'apple_pay,google_pay,visa,master,american_express' | split: ','
	assign pm_enabled = shop.enabled_payment_types
-%}
<div class="{{ classes }}">
	<ul role="list" class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-1.5" aria-label="{{ 'general.payment_marks_label' | t | escape }}">
		{%- for pm_type in pm_types -%}
			{%- if pm_enabled contains pm_type -%}
				<li class="shrink-0">{{ pm_type | payment_type_svg_tag: class: 'block h-6 w-9.5' | replace: '"pi-', pm_id_prefix }}</li>
			{%- endif -%}
		{%- endfor -%}
	</ul>
</div>
